#3703
The Eastward Brick Conduit~
A barrel-vaulted brick conduit bends north from the main junction. The
center channel is slick with runoff, but narrow maintenance ledges
remain passable along either wall. Pale mineral streaks mark old flood
levels far above the present waterline. Small claw marks become more
numerous toward the north, where something has been chewing at the
mortar.
~
