#3704
The Rat-Scratched Conduit~
The masonry here is scarred by thousands of claws. Several bricks have
been gnawed loose around the drainage channel, leaving dark gaps just
large enough for rats to vanish through. A sour animal smell has begun
to overpower the ordinary sewer stink. Northward, the scratching grows
louder and more deliberate.
~
