#3707
The Broken Conduit Junction~
A major section of brickwork has been gnawed through on the western
wall, exposing a cramped earth tunnel beneath the foundations. The
original conduit continues east while the southern line returns toward
the city drain. The breach is not a collapse. Tooth grooves, packed
nesting fiber, and clawed earth make it clear that the rats built their
own road through Midgaard's masonry.
