#3712
A Burrow Under the Masonry~
The rat-made tunnel is too low to stand in comfortably. Packed earth
presses close on every side, reinforced in places with stolen sticks,
strips of leather, and fragments of broken lath. The smell of damp soil
is almost a relief after the sewer, but the constant rustle of bodies
moving through unseen side burrows makes the crawl no safer.
