#3720
The Bat Quarantine Gate~
A stout grate seals the northern pipe. Unlike the rat barrier, this one
was maintained long enough to remain functional. Its bars are scratched
and white-stained, and the flutter of countless wings trembles through
the iron. The city once tried to keep the bat colony confined beyond
this point. Judging by the guano underfoot, that policy was only partly
successful.
~
